/// YamlRepresentable — Protocol for objects that control their own YAML encoding.
///
/// Any class that implements `asYaml` automatically conforms to
/// YamlRepresentable via structural protocol conformance (ADR 0068).
///
/// `Yaml generate:` and `Yaml prettyPrint:` (see `Yaml`) dispatch to `asYaml`
/// for any value that is not one of the natively YAML-representable types
/// (Dictionary, List, String, Integer, Float, Boolean, nil). The returned
/// value is converted recursively, so it may itself contain further
/// YamlRepresentable objects, and is typically a Dictionary with explicit
/// wire-format keys. Mirrors `JsonRepresentable`/`asJson`.
///
/// ## Examples
/// ```beamtalk
/// Value subclass: User
///   field: fullName = ""
///
///   asYaml => #{"full_name" => self.fullName}
/// (User conformsTo: #YamlRepresentable)   // => true
/// ```
Protocol define: YamlRepresentable
  asYaml -> Object
